<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman–Persian Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1514–1823</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ottoman–Iranian wars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars">Persian Wars</a> were the conflicts between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the successive dynasties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavids</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajars</a>, between 1514 and 1823. Fought over eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, they began with the Ottoman victory at Chaldiran and included repeated struggles for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-zuhab">Treaty of Zuhab</a> (1639) roughly fixed the frontier, and the First Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzurum">Erzurum</a> (1823) ended the last war.</p></div>
